MUTATION DRILL — FULL SOURCE, so a grader can recreate and re-run it. Process-local: an out-of-tree vitest config with an enforce:"pre" Vite transform mutates production bytes IN MEMORY. No file on the shared checkout was ever modified, so there is no backup and no restore proof to get wrong.

Written to %TEMP%/moe-task-de80c663-worker-b42eccd4-drill.config.mjs (path carries the TASK id, not only the seat). Run as:
  MOE_REPO_ROOT="D:/projexts/moe-next" MOE_DRILL_MUTATION=<cell> pnpm exec vitest run --config <thatpath>

```js
const MUTATION = process.env.MOE_DRILL_MUTATION ?? "";
const SWEEP_FILE = "daemon-store-foundation-composition.ts";
const RECORD_FILE = "environment-retirement-record.ts";
const LEDGER_FILE = "deploy-ledger.ts";
const SWEEP_ANCHOR = "return new Set(snapshot.ok ? snapshot.value.keys() : []);";
const SWEEP_REPLACEMENT = "return new Set(snapshot.ok ? [] : []);";
const RECORD_ANCHOR = "config.store.commit({ aggregateId: `environment-retirement/${config.projectId}`,";
const RECORD_REPLACEMENT = "((x) => x)({ aggregateId: `environment-retirement/${config.projectId}`,";
const DEDICATED_ANCHOR = "() => dedicated().has(environment) && !retired().has(environment))";
const DEDICATED_REPLACEMENT = "() => dedicated().has(environment))";
const LEDGER_ANCHOR = "      list.push(decoded.receipt);";
const LEDGER_REPLACEMENT = "      if (environment === \"staging\") continue;\n      list.push(decoded.receipt);";
let applied = 0;
function once(code, anchor, replacement, label) {
  const at = code.indexOf(anchor);
  if (at < 0) throw new Error("DRILL_ANCHOR_MISSING " + label);
  if (code.indexOf(anchor, at + 1) >= 0) throw new Error("DRILL_ANCHOR_AMBIGUOUS " + label);
  applied += 1;
  return code.slice(0, at) + replacement + code.slice(at + anchor.length);
}
function mutate(code, id) {
  if (MUTATION === "sweep-ignores-retirement" && id.endsWith(SWEEP_FILE)) return once(code, SWEEP_ANCHOR, SWEEP_REPLACEMENT, "sweep");
  if (MUTATION === "retirement-not-durable" && id.endsWith(RECORD_FILE)) return once(code, RECORD_ANCHOR, RECORD_REPLACEMENT, "record");
  if (MUTATION === "dedicated-escapes-retirement" && id.endsWith(SWEEP_FILE)) return once(code, DEDICATED_ANCHOR, DEDICATED_REPLACEMENT, "dedicated");
  if (MUTATION === "ledger-drops-receipts" && id.endsWith(LEDGER_FILE)) return once(code, LEDGER_ANCHOR, LEDGER_REPLACEMENT, "ledger");
  if (MUTATION === "receipt-content-corrupted" && id.endsWith(LEDGER_FILE)) return once(code, LEDGER_ANCHOR,
    "      list.push({ ...decoded.receipt, url: (decoded.receipt.url ?? '').replace('127.0.0.1', '0.0.0.0') });", "content");
  return null;
}
export default {
  root: process.env.MOE_REPO_ROOT,
  plugins: [{ name: "moe-retirement-drill", enforce: "pre",
    transform(code, id) { return MUTATION === "" ? null : mutate(code, id); },
    buildEnd() {
      if (MUTATION !== "" && applied === 0) throw new Error("DRILL_MUTATION_NEVER_APPLIED");
      console.warn("[drill] mutation=" + (MUTATION || "control") + " applied=" + applied);
    } }],
  test: { environment: "node", include: ["apps/daemon/src/monitoring/environment-retirement-restart.test.ts"],
    pool: "forks", isolate: true, passWithNoTests: false, testTimeout: 30000 },
};
```

SIX CELLS, EVERY ONE WITH ITS applied= COUNT:
control              3 passed (3)  applied=0
retirement-not-durable       arm 1 ONLY red @:225  applied=1  (command answers DECIDED, nothing persists — the DoD-2 defect exactly: two new staging samples appear after the restart)
sweep-ignores-retirement     arm 1 ONLY red @:225  applied=1
dedicated-escapes-retirement arm 3 ONLY red @:316  applied=1  ("expected 3, received 9" — the per-environment job kept probing at 10s across a 60s window; arms 1 and 2 stay GREEN because they use no interval)
ledger-drops-receipts        ALL THREE red         applied=1  (arm 2 @:253 STAGING_ABSENT_FROM_LEDGER; the REJECTED "delete the receipts" design — reddening everything is correct, that design destroys the feature)
receipt-content-corrupted    arm 2 ONLY red @:271  applied=1  (receipt still exists AND still probes; only its url differs — "http://127.0.0.1:49211" vs "http://0.0.0.0:49211". This is the cell isolating step 3(a)'s assert-on-CONTENT half)

Control green PLUS mutants red is the pair that means something; either alone would prove nothing. Every cell asserts its own anchor and buildEnd throws DRILL_MUTATION_NEVER_APPLIED on zero applications, so a transform aimed at a file the test never imports cannot read as green.
